window.magazineEnglish=[
{title:'The evolution of French fashion',sub:'Through history · The art of fashion',body:[['The names that defined luxury','Chanel. Dior. Hermès. Louis Vuitton.'],['Paris sets the stage','The story behind Fashion Week.']],cover:true},
{title:'France, the fashion capital',sub:'Introduction',body:[['','When we think of France, we often picture Paris, the Eiffel Tower, cafés and, of course, fashion! For centuries, France has held an important place in the fashion world. It is known for its elegance, creativity and great couture houses. But French fashion is about more than luxury clothing. It also tells the story of a country, its artists and its traditions.'],['','From Coco Chanel to Christian Dior, French designers have transformed the way we dress. Today, Paris remains an essential destination for fashion enthusiasts. Runway shows, boutiques and new collections attract visitors from around the world. French fashion is much more than a style: it is a true expression of culture.'],['Did you know?','Haute couture is an officially regulated designation in France.']]},
{title:'A journey through the centuries',sub:'The history of French fashion',body:[['The 18th century — Royal fashion','In Marie Antoinette’s time, French fashion was extravagant. Dresses were voluminous, hairstyles impressive and fabrics richly decorated. The court of Versailles influenced the trends of the time.'],['The 19th century — The birth of haute couture','In 1858, Charles Frederick Worth opened a couture house in Paris. He helped transform clothing design into a true artistic profession.'],['The early 20th century — A new freedom','Clothing gradually became more practical. Coco Chanel offered simple, comfortable designs that changed women’s fashion.']]},
{title:'A journey through the centuries',sub:'The history of French fashion',body:[['The 1950s — The return of glamour','Christian Dior transformed fashion with his famous “New Look”, introduced in 1947.'],['The 1960s — A style revolution','Young people embraced modern clothing. Designers experimented with new shapes, materials and colours.'],['Today — Fashion without borders','French fashion continues to evolve through creativity, new technologies and new ideas.']]},
{title:'Every era has its style!',sub:'Fashion through the decades',body:[['The 1920s — Freedom','Dresses became shorter and lighter. Women discovered new ways of dressing.'],['The 1950s — Elegance','Full skirts and defined waists were very popular.'],['The 1960s — Boldness','Bright colours, geometric shapes and new silhouettes defined this decade.'],['The 1980s — Extravagance','Broad shoulders, statement accessories and bold styles attracted attention.'],['','Every decade brings something new. Yet elegance and creativity remain at the heart of French fashion.']]},
{title:'The great fashion houses',sub:'The houses that inspire dreams',body:[['Dior — Dreams and glamour','Founded in 1946, Dior is known for its elegant creations and refined silhouettes. Its famous New Look made fashion history. These two houses show that French fashion can be both classic and innovative.'],['Chanel — Timeless elegance','Founded by Gabrielle Chanel, this house is famous for its tweed suits, quilted bags and Chanel N°5 perfume. France is home to some of the world’s most famous fashion houses. Each has its own history, identity and style. Chanel’s style combines simplicity, elegance and comfort.']]},
{title:'Luxury, the French way',sub:'Tradition meets modernity',body:[['Louis Vuitton — The art of travel','Founded in 1854, Louis Vuitton initially specialised in travel trunks. Today, the house offers luxury bags, clothing, shoes and accessories. It represents the union of tradition and modernity.'],['Hermès — Artisanal expertise','Founded in 1837, Hermès began by making items for horses and their riders. The house later became famous for its leather bags, silk scarves and accessories. It places great importance on quality and craftsmanship.'],['What makes these houses special?','Their success rests on three elements: a strong history, exceptional craftsmanship and a recognisable identity. Together, they contribute to the international reputation of French fashion.']]},
{title:'Coco Chanel (1883–1971)',sub:'Famous designers · The visionaries of fashion',body:[['','Behind every famous creation is a person with ideas, imagination and a vision. Some designers have influenced fashion so deeply that their ideas remain popular decades later.'],['The queen of simplicity','Gabrielle “Coco” Chanel is one of the most influential designers of the 20th century. At a time when women’s clothing was often complicated, she proposed simpler, more comfortable fashion. She popularised the little black dress, tweed suits and costume jewellery. For Chanel, a woman could be elegant while remaining free to move.'],['Her iconic creations','The little black dress. The tweed suit. Chanel N°5 perfume. The quilted 2.55 bag.']]},
{title:'Dior and Saint Laurent',sub:'Two designers, two revolutions',body:[['Christian Dior (1905–1957) — The master of the New Look','Christian Dior founded his couture house in 1946. In 1947, he presented a collection that transformed women’s fashion. The New Look featured defined waists, full skirts and elegant silhouettes. After the Second World War, his designs brought a new image of luxury. Dior quickly became a symbol of Parisian glamour.'],['Yves Saint Laurent (1936–2008) — The bold designer','Yves Saint Laurent is known for his modern, original style. In 1961, he founded his fashion house with Pierre Bergé. In 1966, he introduced Le Smoking, a women’s tuxedo inspired by men’s tailoring. He also drew on art and different cultures to create unique clothing. His designs helped change the conventions of women’s fashion.']]},
{title:'Paris Fashion Week',sub:'Two designers, two revolutions',body:[['','Imagine Paris during Fashion Week: photographers, models, journalists and designers gather in the French capital. Paris Fashion Week is one of the most important events in fashion. It allows houses to present their new collections to the press, buyers and industry professionals.'],['','Modern Paris Fashion Week has been organised since 1974. Today, women’s and men’s ready-to-wear presentations take place at different times of year. Paris also hosts Haute Couture Week, dedicated to exceptional creations.'],['Why is this event important?','Fashion Week introduces new trends, showcases designers and celebrates creativity. It also shows that fashion is an art as well as an international industry.']]},
{title:'Behind the scenes of a fashion show',sub:'From an idea to the runway',body:[['','A fashion show seems magical. Yet behind a few minutes of spectacle lie weeks, sometimes months, of preparation.'],['1. Inspiration','The big moment: everything begins with an idea. Designers find inspiration in art, travel, nature or history.'],['2. Creation','Designers draw sketches and choose fabrics, colours and accessories.'],['3. Preparations','Teams organise fittings, hairstyling, makeup and music.'],['4. The big moment','Models present the clothes on the runway in front of the guests.'],['5. After the show','Photographs and videos circulate in magazines and on social media.'],['Did you know?','A fashion show is more than a presentation of clothing. Music, lighting and set design also contribute to the atmosphere of the spectacle.']]},
{title:'French fashion reinvents itself',sub:'French fashion today',body:[['','French fashion never stands still. It evolves with new generations and changes in society. Today, designers explore new materials, original silhouettes and different production methods.'],['More responsible fashion','Many brands are interested in recycled materials, second-hand clothes and reducing waste.'],['Technology and fashion','Digital tools make it possible to create designs, prepare collections and present clothing in new ways.'],['The influence of social media','Instagram, videos and content creators allow trends to spread rapidly around the world.'],['Freedom of style','Young people mix vintage clothing, modern pieces and personal accessories to create their own identity.'],['','French fashion thus continues to combine tradition, creativity and innovation.']]},
{title:'From Paris to the whole world',sub:'The global influence of French fashion',body:[['','French fashion does not stop at France’s borders. It inspires designers, artists and fashion enthusiasts around the world. It travels through images, magazines, films and social media. It continues to influence the way people dress and express their personalities.'],['Fashion and celebrities','Artists and celebrities often wear French creations at international events, helping make the great French fashion houses known around the world.'],['Fashion and cinema','Costumes play an important role in films. Clothes can tell a story, represent an era or show a character’s personality.'],['An international influence','The great French houses present their collections in several countries. Their creations are admired by people from different cultures.'],['Paris, a source of inspiration','The streets of Paris, its monuments, museums and architecture inspire photographers and designers.']]},
{title:'French fashion: a story that continues',sub:'Conclusion',body:[['','Over the centuries, French fashion has undergone many transformations. From royal dresses to modern designs, every era has brought new ideas and new styles.'],['','Designers such as Coco Chanel, Christian Dior and Yves Saint Laurent changed fashion history through their imagination and boldness. The great couture houses continue to preserve their expertise while exploring new trends.'],['','Paris Fashion Week also brings French creations to the world. This journey through fashion shows that a garment can tell a story, represent a culture and express a personality.'],['','Fashion evolves, but creativity remains essential.'],['“Fashion passes; creativity remains.”','— Our final reflection'],['','French fashion is not only a story of clothes. It is a story of art, culture, freedom and imagination.']]},
{title:'The little fashion dictionary',sub:'Words from the world of style',dictionary:true,body:[['Fashion','Clothing styles that are popular in a particular era.'],['A designer','Someone who imagines and designs clothes.'],['Haute couture','The creation of luxury, made-to-measure clothing.'],['Ready-to-wear','Clothing made in standard sizes.'],['A fashion show','An event where models present clothes.'],['A collection','A set of clothes created for a season.'],['A couture house','A company specialising in fashion design.'],['A model','A person who presents clothes.'],['A trend','A style popular at a particular time.'],['A silhouette','The overall shape of an outfit.'],['Fabric','A material used to make clothing.'],['An accessory','An item that completes an outfit.'],['Elegance','A quality associated with style and refinement.'],['Luxury','High-quality, often expensive products.'],['Craftsmanship','The knowledge and skills needed for a task.'],['Embroidery','Decoration made with thread on fabric.'],['An atelier','A place where craftspeople and designers work.'],['A sketch','A quick drawing representing an idea.'],['A skirt','A garment worn around the waist.'],['A dress','A garment covering the upper body and extending over the legs.']]},
{title:'Credits and acknowledgements',sub:'A collective creation',credits:true,body:[['','This magazine was created as a group project devoted to the evolution of French fashion. Every team member contributed to research, writing, design and production.'],['Editorial team',''],['Member 1 — Saanvi Subhash','Research and writing: introduction, the history of French fashion and its evolution through the decades.'],['Member 2 — Vriddhi Bantiya','Research and writing: great fashion houses, French luxury and famous designers.'],['Member 3 — Samriddhi Bhushan','Research and writing: Christian Dior, Yves Saint Laurent and Paris Fashion Week.'],['Member 4 — Shaurya Chauhan','Research and writing: behind the scenes of fashion shows, contemporary fashion and international influence.'],['Member 5 — Ishant Meena','Research and writing: conclusion, fashion dictionary, bibliography and content verification.'],['Art direction and design','Three members of our team created the visual design and layout: Saanvi Subhash — art direction and visual identity. Samriddhi Bhushan — layout and organisation of photographs. Vriddhi Bantiya — typography, colours and graphic finishing.'],['Design tool','Canva — design and production of the digital magazine.'],['Thank you for reading!','Fashion is an evolving art, but creativity is shared.']]}
];
